diff --git a/scripts/README_intention_ablation.md b/scripts/README_intention_ablation.md
index 69cdb2e..3c5d00a 100644
--- a/scripts/README_intention_ablation.md
+++ b/scripts/README_intention_ablation.md
@@ -173,3 +173,34 @@ controlled rollout. This encoder is task-specific and is **not** pretrained
 CLIP or an unseen-language generalization test. The run does not mask text;
 compare it with the original no-text checkpoint and test wrong-task text to
 establish that the head actually uses the instruction.
+
+### Gripper state and transition supervision
+
+New runs default to `--gripper-state-source causal`: use measured gripper
+observations when available, otherwise the **previous** executed action command.
+The first frame uses the episode `initial_gripper` attribute (default 0). Neither
+the current action label nor a future command enters the state. This applies to
+dense and sparse cached loaders. Gripper commands use 0=closed, 1=open.
+
+The default remains uniform sampling (`--gripper-transition-fraction 0`).
+Opt-in `--gripper-transition-fraction 0.25` reserves up to one quarter of episode
+training anchors for actual consecutive-command changes. Remaining anchors are
+sampled without replacement from the rest of the episode, retaining the same
+supervision budget. Episodes with few/no switches automatically use more uniform
+anchors. Validation stays uniformly sampled. This is an experimental learning
+setting; compare transition recall **and** false switches, not just overall
+accuracy. Use `--gripper-transition-fraction 0` for the uniform control or crop
+sampling.
+
+Old ablation manifests predate this contract. To reproduce/resume their behavior,
+explicitly pass `--gripper-state-source legacy_zero --gripper-transition-fraction 0`.
+A fresh output directory is required for a corrected-input training comparison;
+resume rejects silently changing these settings. Old weights are not repaired by
+changing the loader. `--evaluate-existing` preserves the manifest's convention,
+including the legacy default when metadata is absent.
+
+Compression experiments should start with `--variants no_intent_no_memory
+--use-task-text`, changing only `--compressed-dim 8`, `16`, or `32` and using
+separate output directories. Full training and closed-loop evaluation are needed
+to select a width; short pilot errors are not simulator success rates. The flat
+memory architecture grows much faster with width than this plain baseline.
